// BUG-798 (2026-08-17): `vrp_widen_loop_addr_taken` was a hand-rolled if/else
// chain that did not name NODE_SPAWN — and whose trailing comment asserted
// spawn/await/asm were leaves with "no `&` subtree", which is false. So
// `spawn bump(&i)` in a loop body did not widen `i`'s range while the plain-call
// control `bump(&i)` did, and `a[i]` earlier in the body was proven against the
// stale pre-loop range: ASan-confirmed silent stack-buffer-overflow write.
//
// The walker is now an exhaustive no-`default:` switch, so a NEW NodeKind that
// can hold `&x` is a BUILD FAILURE rather than another silently-missed alias.
//
// VALUE-ASSERTING: guard present => early return 0; guard absent => 42.
// Measured against a from-HEAD pre-fix build: 42 before, 0 after.
void bump(*u32 p) { *p += 9; }

u32 probe() {
    u8[4] a;
    u32 i = 0;
    for (u32 q = 0; q < 2; q += 1) {
        a[i] = 1;
        ThreadHandle th = spawn bump(&i);
        th.join();
    }
    return 42;
}

u32 main() { return probe(); }
